<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RBM mode's gear for Commander Battle's Khuzait troop classes (cb_mpclassdivisions_khuzait.xml), read by
  CommanderBattle/RbmLoadouts.cs (the format is in its header). Light mode keeps the classes' mp_ gear and never reads
  this file. Same rules as the mp_ characters (cb_mpcharacters_khuzait.xml):
  - Bots draw every slot from a random roster, so each slot holds the same kind of item in every roster: the rosters
    vary the looks (armour and helmets of one tier, shields of one size and kind), never the loadout.
  - Slots: Item0 main weapon (or bow), Item1 shield (or arrows), Item2 sidearm, Item3 free. Horse archers carry no
    shield. A Cape (shoulders) slot is used by the medium and heavy classes, in every roster. Mounted classes have a
    horse and a harness in the hero and every roster; foot classes have none.
  - Setups mirror the class's weapon setup perks by index (index 0, the class's own loadout, has none): the same slots,
    with the closest singleplayer item of the same weapon class. Sidearm rule as in the mp_ data: spears and lances keep
    the sabre (the lancers a mace), the sabres and the swung glaive clear it; the glaive also clears the shield.
  - Doctrine: horse-archer culture and lancers with tough small steppe shields (the plain ids: RBM's kalkan-strapped
    copies use RBM's own holsters, which multiplayer doesn't load, and RBM itself maps them back to these with its
    default settings); the weakest infantry (wicker or small round shields, no pikes) and the lightest foot
    archers. No throwing weapons.
  - Gear tiers: light = levy and nomads (suede, mirrored or studded leather, a real steppe helmet); medium = men-at-arms
    (strapped lamellar, stitched or studded leather over aketon, light shoulders, lamellar helmets); heavy = the khan's
    guard (bronze lamellar over mail, lancer lamellar, noble lancer helmets, the best bows, lances and horses).
  - Items only from the singleplayer and RBM item files that RBM.Multiplayer loads (RBM's versions carry RBM's stats),
    mostly the ids RBM's troop overhaul (RBMXML/RBMCombat_unit_overhaul.xml) gives these troops. No mp_ items.
  - Seeded from RBM's overhaul:
      mp_light_infantry_khuzait (nomad spearman)        khuzait_nomad, khuzait_footman
      mp_heavy_infantry_khuzait (darkhan)               khuzait_spearman, khuzait_spear_infantry
      mp_light_ranged_khuzait (steppe archer)           khuzait_hunter, khuzait_tribal_warrior
      mp_heavy_ranged_khuzait (marksman)                khuzait_marksman, khuzait_archer
      mp_light_cavalry_khuzait (nomad rider)            khuzait_horseman
      mp_horse_archer_khuzait (nomad horse archer)      khuzait_raider
      mp_heavy_cavalry_khuzait (kheshig)                khuzait_heavy_lancer, khuzait_lancer
      cb_heavy_horse_archer_khuzait (khan's guard)      khuzait_khans_guard, khuzait_heavy_horse_archer, khuzait_kheshig
      cb_general_khuzait (noyan and torguud)            khuzait_heavy_lancer (weapons), khuzait_khans_guard (armour)
-->
